# Carbon-dioxide concentration of a gas, as an amount-of-substance fraction.
# Minted because the OpenCyphal standard set has no concentration sample type
# (ADR-0005 d2).
#
# An NDIR instrument measures a mole fraction; ppm IS that fraction scaled by
# 1e6. The scaling is dropped on the wire for the reason ADR-0005 rev 1 gave for
# joule over watt-hour -- the node would multiply a raw count by a constant
# either way, and float32 relative precision is unaffected. The 400 ppm ambient
# baseline of M01 spec 6.3 is 400e-6 here.
#
# Depletion below the sensor's specified band is reported, not clamped: M01
# spec 6.3 makes below-400 ppm a real operating condition of a closed cabinet
# during photoperiod, outside the specified accuracy but not outside the range.
uavcan.time.SynchronizedTimestamp.1.0 timestamp
float32 mole_fraction  # mol CO2 per mol of gas; 400 ppm = 400e-6
@extent 16 * 8
